                      P·R·O·U·D·L·Y·? P·R·E·S·E·N·T·S

                     BullView v1.0a by nIKE/cRAZE^5150

Description.
~~~~~~~~~~~~
Bulletin Viewer. Let's the sysop have all bulletins in one directory instead
of the same files in XX directorys (hehe)..
Quite fast (95% E, 5% Asm :)), Goodlooking (as me), easy to install.
Btw, this door may not be used by RHYS/DELIRIUM. I think he should know why!

Installing this damn door:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Copy "Bull" To any directory on your HD.
Copy the icon (B.Info) to BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/ and edit it to set your needs.
Stack needs at least 3000 bytes, 4000 recommended
Type = XIM.

Make a directory called BBS:Bulletins and copy "Bullhelp", and the other files
included to it. Edit the files to set your needs (easy to understand?!)
Filenames should be Bull<Nr>.Txt<.Gr> where <Nr> is the number of the bulletin.

On each line in Bullhelp to be the bulletin number you want.
That means, Line 1=Bulletin 1, line 7=bulletin 7 etc..
Look at the Bullhelp file included for more info!

To be able to let the user update the bulletins, u'll have to make an ordinary
dos script that does it. Copy the file to S: and call it "Up"....BullView will
Execute this if the user wants to update the bulletins!

